#{[17592186101585 #edb/ref 1061 1142 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101585 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "97a0a8f1-3fcd-5681-9176-f997a3d0c81b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101585 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186100812 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101607 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186101756 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101607 #edb/ref 1061 12338 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101607 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "060c1ce4-0c9d-5214-85ce-1b51fedd7791" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101607 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186101942 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101608 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186101755 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101608 #edb/ref 1061 12339 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101608 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "22f4b88d-3d39-5cdb-8f96-eef99b7f8d43" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101608 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186100827 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101609 #edb/ref 1061 12340 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101609 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "822556de-6ecc-5575-befa-a8d021246130" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101609 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186100828 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101755 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186101609 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101755 #edb/ref 1061 22970 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101755 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9b64bab5-b9b1-5d61-9e9d-6f44ed48f4e9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101755 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186100919 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101756 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186101608 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101756 #edb/ref 1061 22971 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101756 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9694c0be-fabb-57e1-9b70-9ee9fc1f9bdc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101756 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186100920 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101942 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's suppose we only know the values of the functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ at $x=0$ along with their derivatives, as given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $g(x)$ | $f'(x)$ | $g'(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n\nCan we calculate $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\Big( f(x)g(x)\\Big )$ at $x=0?$\n\nUsing the product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\Big( f(x)g(x)\\Big) = f'(x)g(x)+f(x)g'(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=0,$ this gives\n\n$$\n\\left.\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\Big( f(x)g(x)\\Big) \\right|_{x=0}\t=\tf'(0)g(0)+f(0)g'(0).\n$$\n\nAll of these values are given in the table! So, substituting the values from the table into the formula, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))|}_{x=0} & ={f}^{′}(0)g(0)+f(0){g}^{′}(0) \\\\  & =4\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =22.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101942 #edb/ref 1065 2627 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101942 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "9df0b4fa-df54-5f34-9bdc-3fc11befd2e8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101942 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101997 #edb/ref 1064 "The function $f(x)$ is differentiable on an open interval containing $x=2$. The values of $f$ and $f'$ are given in the following table:\n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $f'(x)$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $2$ | $0$ | $4$ |\n\nLet's find\n\n$$\n\\lim\\limits_{x \\to 2} \\dfrac{f(x)}{x^3-8}\n$$\n\nNotice that if we try to substitute $x=2$ directly into the limit, we reach the indeterminate form\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{0}{0}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nlim_(x → 2)(f(x))/(x^{3} - 8) &= \\left.(f(x))/(x^{3} - 8)\\right|_{x = 2} \\\\\n&= (f(2))/(2^{3} - 8) \\\\\n&= \\frac{0}{8 - 8} \\\\\n&= \\frac{0}{0}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we use L'Hopital's rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nlim_(x → 2)(f(x))/(x^{3} - 8) &= lim_(x → 2)((f(x))^{′})/((x^{3} - 8)^{′}) \\\\\n&= lim_(x → 2)(f^{′}(x))/(3x^{2})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute $x=2$ again, and this time, we are able to determine the result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nlim_(x → 2)(f^{′}(x))/(3x^{2}) &= \\left.(f^{′}(x))/(3x^{2})\\right|_{x = 2} \\\\\n&= (f^{′}(2))/(3 \\cdot 2^{2}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{4}{3 \\cdot 2^{2} - 0} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\lim\\limits_{x \\to 2} \\dfrac{f(x)}{x^3-8}=\\dfrac{1}{3}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101997 #edb/ref 1065 599 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101997 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "c8d2f073-f126-5950-9555-61f8a6dd159a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101997 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105862 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048593 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105862 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186106357 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105862 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186106482 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105862 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186106483 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105862 #edb/ref 1039 "Applying the Chain Rule With the Power Rule" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105862 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186105446 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105862 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "55d07843-4356-52c7-80c0-0fcadbb2ff9f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105863 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186051084 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105863 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186106058 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105863 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186106059 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105863 #edb/ref 1039 "Applying the Chain Rule Given Data For Two Functions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105863 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186105447 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105863 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "7ca934a6-9d97-5918-a35b-d823f1e7a22a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105864 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050789 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105864 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186106358 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105864 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186106547 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105864 #edb/ref 1039 "Applying the Chain Rule With Trigonometric Functions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105864 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186105448 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105864 #edb/ref